---
// The documented limits, said once and reused. Wording must stay true to the README's "Known limitations".
---
<ul class="plain-list">
  <li><strong>Google decides what the panel shows.</strong> An AI Overview sometimes appears and often doesn't. DNDReader does not promise one.</li>
  <li><strong>You can't sign in to Google in the panel.</strong> Google blocks sign-in inside embedded browsers, so results are signed out and not personalised.</li>
  <li><strong>A consent screen can appear in the panel, and occasionally a CAPTCHA.</strong> You deal with it there, as you would in any browser.</li>
  <li><strong>Looking something up needs an internet connection.</strong> Reading a PDF does not.</li>
  <li><strong>Text-based PDFs only.</strong> A scanned page has no text to select, and there is no OCR.</li>
</ul>
